       "part_of.note": "T-1980. Names a relation between two buildings and never a person: the fort's barn is part of the post, a tannery's shed part of the tannery. Every name it quotes \u2014 the source's author, the firm, the homestead's owner \u2014 is one the same record's function.note or the principal's own occupants block already carries, and those ARE read, so reading this note again would add no name the town has not said something about and could only let a quotation take a man out of the deal.",
